#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262689 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b509b42a-c38a-5400-8f93-f3e9024b16a2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Coordinates of a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e65ccbe8-17b2-513b-9c6d-7df15d59c38a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e65ccbe8-17b2-513b-9c6d-7df15d59c38a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262691} :answer-field/id #uuid "faa15742-bd4f-5848-8190-594cdb8404cb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262690} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "107b7268-e9ae-57e2-87ca-690b66d51b73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "107b7268-e9ae-57e2-87ca-690b66d51b73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262693} :answer-field/id #uuid "e48e5b88-1909-5ce0-b9a5-534da8fa87b6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262692}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8335de10-730d-56df-a953-7cf72e8b6a76" :question/math-academy-id "q-167788" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949061/assets/d868c69cee832cad796feaf0aae5bd6a4bd04d9ab2e76e275bb6e441a429f6e4.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above.\n\nCurrent part:\n\nWhat are the $xy$-coordinates of the point $A?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A\\,($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the coordinates of the point, we inspect its position along the $x$- and $y$-axes.\n\n* The point is $3$ units to the *right* of the origin, in the *positive* direction of the $x$-axis. So, its $x$-coordinate is $3.$\n\n* The point is $2$ units *below* the origin, in the *negative* direction of the $y$-axis. So, its $y$-coordinate is $-2.$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of our point are $(3,-2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262694 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf635847-145c-5da5-927e-8196e809324e" :knowledge-point/title "Points Associated With Horizontal and Vertical Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17d8dbc4-22f5-587a-9c41-e4232f06d39a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17d8dbc4-22f5-587a-9c41-e4232f06d39a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262696} :answer-field/id #uuid "b07373f9-6740-5181-8169-b9504056d454" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262695} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5cc837c-0b4b-5767-a210-64fac28852c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5cc837c-0b4b-5767-a210-64fac28852c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262698} :answer-field/id #uuid "509153a4-9ac3-578d-8fa0-40cb26fa7ca0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262697}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ffb79773-c313-53b8-a450-7ccc3d8a8f98" :question/math-academy-id "q-167789" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949061/assets/d868c69cee832cad796feaf0aae5bd6a4bd04d9ab2e76e275bb6e441a429f6e4.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nWhat are the $xy$-coordinates of the point $A?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A\\,($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nWrite the equations of the vertical and horizontal lines that pass through the point $B.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The **equation** of the vertical line is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The **equation** of the horizontal line is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of $B$ are $(1,4).$\n\n* Since the vertical line should pass through $(1,4)$, the $x$-value for every point on the line is $1.$ Hence, the equation of that line is \n\n$$\nx=1.\n$$\n\n* Since the horizontal line should pass through $(1,4)$, the $y$-value for every point on the line is $4.$ Hence, the equation of that line is \n\n$$\ny=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5df52cb5-75b1-58d9-8535-07c1bb87be34" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Length of a Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a2b9ba1-e375-5c18-ad02-fb0b50b4bba4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a2b9ba1-e375-5c18-ad02-fb0b50b4bba4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262701} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e46eb46-b2a5-5ade-883b-641cfbd4681f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262700}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6c9d7404-0998-5f8d-97f0-3177d285e62d" :question/math-academy-id "q-167790" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949061/assets/d868c69cee832cad796feaf0aae5bd6a4bd04d9ab2e76e275bb6e441a429f6e4.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nWhat are the $xy$-coordinates of the point $A?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A\\,($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nWrite the equations of the vertical and horizontal lines that pass through the point $B.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The **equation** of the vertical line is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $x=1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The **equation** of the horizontal line is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $y=4$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nWhat is the length of $\\overset{―}{AB}?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $|\\overset{―}{AB}|\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the picture, the points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(3,-2)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(1,4),$ respectively.\n\nTo find the length of $\\overset{―}{AB},$ we use the distance formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{―}{AB}| & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1-3)^{2}+(4-(-2))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{40} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262702 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2db034b8-5119-5cf3-bb6e-e6c79d024177" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope Given Two Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb342551-51d1-5d90-8991-2ea64d0849f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb342551-51d1-5d90-8991-2ea64d0849f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262704} :answer-field/id #uuid "65cb04fc-8d79-58ef-b7f5-2eb39e7ae65b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262703}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ce71f011-bdf9-52a9-bba7-32d8bf5cf680" :question/math-academy-id "q-167791" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949061/assets/d868c69cee832cad796feaf0aae5bd6a4bd04d9ab2e76e275bb6e441a429f6e4.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nWhat are the $xy$-coordinates of the point $A?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A\\,($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nWrite the equations of the vertical and horizontal lines that pass through the point $B.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The **equation** of the vertical line is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $x=1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The **equation** of the horizontal line is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $y=4$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nWhat is the length of $\\overset{―}{AB}?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $|\\overset{―}{AB}|\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2\\sqrt{10}$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nWhat is the slope $m$ of the line $\\overset{↔}{AB}?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $m\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "As we found previously, the points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(3,-2)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(1,4),$ respectively.\n\nTherefore, we compute the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-(-2)}{1-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{-2} \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262705 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e985ae8-05ba-590a-b504-4c84884679f4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Line That Passes Through Two Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6546e8e6-3cc4-52af-b374-2f242c745f33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6546e8e6-3cc4-52af-b374-2f242c745f33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262707} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9d9e9e1-9eff-5ebc-a07e-ef88845566fc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262706} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64db0ae7-03f7-53e6-929b-65511eebeac3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64db0ae7-03f7-53e6-929b-65511eebeac3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262709} :answer-field/id #uuid "2885e888-50fc-59b5-84a0-b81e7a737c9f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262708}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "339e5607-8b24-5ab3-93c4-985cb0c570be" :question/math-academy-id "q-167792" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949061/assets/d868c69cee832cad796feaf0aae5bd6a4bd04d9ab2e76e275bb6e441a429f6e4.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nWhat are the $xy$-coordinates of the point $A?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A\\,($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nWrite the equations of the vertical and horizontal lines that pass through the point $B.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The **equation** of the vertical line is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $x=1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The **equation** of the horizontal line is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $y=4$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nWhat is the length of $\\overset{―}{AB}?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $|\\overset{―}{AB}|\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2\\sqrt{10}$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nWhat is the slope $m$ of the line $\\overset{↔}{AB}?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $m\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-3$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the $y$-intercept of $\\overset{↔}{AB},$ and express the equation of this line in slope-intercept form.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The $y$-intercept of the line is $b\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The equation is $y\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nAs we found previously, the slope is $m=-3.$\n\nSubstituting $m=-3$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-3x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(3,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x+b \\\\ -2 & =-3(3)+b \\\\ -2 & =-9+b \\\\ 7 & =b \\\\ b & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-3x+7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262710 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dd738be-308a-54b8-aa4c-7acd6d60b691" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Inequality Corresponding to a Given Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c664c57-5d1c-50cb-85be-32ba63ab3bcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c664c57-5d1c-50cb-85be-32ba63ab3bcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262712} :answer-field/id #uuid "56e63261-5563-554b-8791-701c7dac6377" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262711}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ac666e1c-2909-5180-bd5b-f00362a74cc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-167793" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949061/assets/d868c69cee832cad796feaf0aae5bd6a4bd04d9ab2e76e275bb6e441a429f6e4.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nWhat are the $xy$-coordinates of the point $A?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A\\,($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nWrite the equations of the vertical and horizontal lines that pass through the point $B.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The **equation** of the vertical line is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $x=1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The **equation** of the horizontal line is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $y=4$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nWhat is the length of $\\overset{―}{AB}?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $|\\overset{―}{AB}|\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2\\sqrt{10}$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nWhat is the slope $m$ of the line $\\overset{↔}{AB}?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $m\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-3$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nFind the $y$-intercept of $\\overset{↔}{AB},$ and express the equation of this line in slope-intercept form.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The $y$-intercept of the line is $b\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $7$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The equation is $y\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-3x+7$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nWhat is the inequality that defines the shaded region?\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $y$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$-3x+7$" :question/worked-solution "Previously we found that the line $\\overset{↔}{AB}$ has the equation\n\n$$\ny=-3x+7.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to decide which inequality symbol to use. \n\n* Since the line is *dashed*, we will use a *strict* inequality. \n\n* Since the shaded region is *below* the line, the inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* those on the line.\n\nTherefore, the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<-3x+7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262713 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63461668-4f76-52a4-8115-1ab135eef9e3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the X-Intercept of a Line Given a Point and a Slope"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d5cd928-2d0d-540e-af3b-c7b79fa061eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d5cd928-2d0d-540e-af3b-c7b79fa061eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262715} :answer-field/id #uuid "43be6fdd-061f-58aa-ba82-40c1959331fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262714}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "376ae008-bb20-5a62-909c-6d69d1a50468" :question/math-academy-id "q-167794" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949061/assets/d868c69cee832cad796feaf0aae5bd6a4bd04d9ab2e76e275bb6e441a429f6e4.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nWhat are the $xy$-coordinates of the point $A?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A\\,($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nWrite the equations of the vertical and horizontal lines that pass through the point $B.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The **equation** of the vertical line is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $x=1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The **equation** of the horizontal line is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $y=4$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nWhat is the length of $\\overset{―}{AB}?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $|\\overset{―}{AB}|\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2\\sqrt{10}$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nWhat is the slope $m$ of the line $\\overset{↔}{AB}?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $m\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-3$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nFind the $y$-intercept of $\\overset{↔}{AB},$ and express the equation of this line in slope-intercept form.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The $y$-intercept of the line is $b\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $7$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The equation is $y\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-3x+7$\n\nEarlier part 6:\n\nWhat is the inequality that defines the shaded region?\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $y$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $<$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$-3x+7$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nCalculate the $x$-intercept of the line $\\overset{↔}{AB}.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Previously, we found that $\\overset{↔}{AB}$ has equation\n\n$$\ny=-3x+7.\n$$\n\nAt the $x$-intercept, the $y$-coordinate is equal to $0.$ So, we can substitute $y=0$ into the equation and then solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x+7 \\\\ 0 & =-3x+7 \\\\ -7 & =-3x \\\\ \\frac{-7}{-3} & =\\frac{-3x}{-3} \\\\ \\frac{7}{3} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $x=\\frac{7}{3}.$ The coordinates of the $x$-intercept are $(\\frac{7}{3},0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f399f6ed-91bc-594e-9a40-b7c79f60c5dc" :knowledge-point/title "Converting from Slope-Intercept Form to Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "935b1b00-a0d0-5a5a-b9f5-eb5cc929969c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+y=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "935b1b00-a0d0-5a5a-b9f5-eb5cc929969c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+y=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262718} :answer-field/id #uuid "831d354a-dc73-5ac0-a4f3-002e3c3fd9f4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262717}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "76e9cc3b-f993-58c1-a836-10d0e9f14cb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-167795" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949061/assets/d868c69cee832cad796feaf0aae5bd6a4bd04d9ab2e76e275bb6e441a429f6e4.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nWhat are the $xy$-coordinates of the point $A?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A\\,($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nWrite the equations of the vertical and horizontal lines that pass through the point $B.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The **equation** of the vertical line is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $x=1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The **equation** of the horizontal line is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $y=4$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nWhat is the length of $\\overset{―}{AB}?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $|\\overset{―}{AB}|\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2\\sqrt{10}$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nWhat is the slope $m$ of the line $\\overset{↔}{AB}?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $m\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-3$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nFind the $y$-intercept of $\\overset{↔}{AB},$ and express the equation of this line in slope-intercept form.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The $y$-intercept of the line is $b\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $7$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The equation is $y\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-3x+7$\n\nEarlier part 6:\n\nWhat is the inequality that defines the shaded region?\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $y$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $<$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$-3x+7$\n\nEarlier part 7:\n\nCalculate the $x$-intercept of the line $\\overset{↔}{AB}.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{7}{3}$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nWrite the equation of $\\overset{↔}{AB}$ in standard form.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The equation is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Our goal is to write the equation in the form \n\n$$\nax+by=c,\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,$ and $c$ are integers with no common factors and $a\\ge 0.$\n\nWe begin by moving all of the variables to the left-hand side and all of the constants to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x+7 \\\\ 3x+y & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $a,b,$ and $c$ are integers with no common factors, and $a\\ge 0.$ So, we are done!\n\nThe standard form of the line is \n\n$$\n3x+y=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262719 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44b9b212-27c4-5d6d-a221-cd85c25fc956" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Line Perpendicular to a Line Through Two Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b32c641e-0854-54f6-9509-f606969d5e30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}x-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b32c641e-0854-54f6-9509-f606969d5e30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}x-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262721} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f035074-9341-50eb-9d73-2f9e66d75a6c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262720}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0e801809-f356-5fe9-8297-e3c4cd79b231" :question/math-academy-id "q-167797" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949061/assets/d868c69cee832cad796feaf0aae5bd6a4bd04d9ab2e76e275bb6e441a429f6e4.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nWhat are the $xy$-coordinates of the point $A?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A\\,($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nWrite the equations of the vertical and horizontal lines that pass through the point $B.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The **equation** of the vertical line is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $x=1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The **equation** of the horizontal line is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $y=4$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nWhat is the length of $\\overset{―}{AB}?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $|\\overset{―}{AB}|\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2\\sqrt{10}$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nWhat is the slope $m$ of the line $\\overset{↔}{AB}?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $m\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-3$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nFind the $y$-intercept of $\\overset{↔}{AB},$ and express the equation of this line in slope-intercept form.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The $y$-intercept of the line is $b\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $7$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The equation is $y\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-3x+7$\n\nEarlier part 6:\n\nWhat is the inequality that defines the shaded region?\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $y$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $<$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$-3x+7$\n\nEarlier part 7:\n\nCalculate the $x$-intercept of the line $\\overset{↔}{AB}.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{7}{3}$\n\nEarlier part 8:\n\nWrite the equation of $\\overset{↔}{AB}$ in standard form.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The equation is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3x+y=7$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nWrite the equation of the line that passes through the point $(3,-5)$ and is perpendicular to $\\overset{↔}{AB}.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The slope-intercept form of the equation is $y\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Perpendicular lines have slopes that are negative reciprocals of each other. Therefore, since $\\overset{↔}{AB}$ has the slope $m=-3,$ our perpendicular line must have a slope of \n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(-3)}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, our perpendicular line has the slope ${m}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}$ and passes through the point $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(3,-5).$ \n\nFinally, using point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & ={m}_{1}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-5) & =\\frac{1}{3}(x-3) \\\\ y+5 & =\\frac{1}{3}x-1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}x-6\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
